  Checked exceptions are those that must be either handled or declared in the method signature. 
  ClassNotFoundException is a checked exception , 
  because it indicates a failure to find a class at runtime, 
  which can be anticipated and should be properly managed by developers.

Example-01 
package Proj_01;

public class CheckedExcetion_Example01 {

	public static void main(String[] args)  {
		// TODO Auto-generated method stub
		//Unhandled exception type ClassNotFoundException | red cross on line number-08
		 Class.forName("Proj_01.Example_01");
		}
}
line number - 15 is a compile time exception 

Causes
ClassNotFoundException is thrown when the JVM cannot find a specified class in the classpath, 
often due to incorrect paths or missing libraries.
This exception can also occur when using reflection to load classes dynamically, and the specified class does not exist.




    
